{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"Meaningful coverage requires a real SQL Server and its separate JDBC driver.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n      \"coordinate\": \"com.microsoft.sqlserver:mssql-jdbc:12.2.0.jre11\",\n      \"scope\": \"testImplementation\",\n      \"reason\": \"flyway-sqlserver does not provide the JDBC driver transitively; Flyway documents it as a separate dependency. The existing test already resolves this driver.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"docker_image\",\n      \"image\": \"mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest\",\n      \"slug\": \"mssql-server\",\n      \"reason\": \"SQL Server-specific Flyway behavior cannot be meaningfully exercised against an embedded database; reuse the existing pinned SQL Server image.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Start SQL Server with EULA acceptance and a strong SA password, wait for readiness on port 1433, and configure the JDBC URL, database, username, and password consistently for JVM and native tests. Preserve -H:+AddAllCharsets because the SQL Server driver selects code pages from server collation.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"The reported failure already occurs after native-image creation and already includes -H:+AddAllCharsets; setup alone will not fix the runtime metadata failure.\",\n    \"Container startup timing and SQL Server authentication may make tests flaky without an explicit readiness wait.\"\n  ]\n}"}}
